    sidebar: [
        "WEATHER: Cascadia expects rain, followed by rain. A sunbreak is possible next month. Residents urged not to panic.",
        "WEATHER: Grain Belt winds out of the south at 40 mph, which locals call \"a nice drying day.\"",
        "WEATHER: Colorado: sunny, snow, sunny, hail, sunny. All before lunch. Dress in layers.",
        "WEATHER: Phoenix reports \"a dry heat\" for the 200th day in a row. Forecasters have stopped saying the number.",
        "WEATHER: Inversion settles over Salt Lake. Biscuit recommends the ski slopes, where it's sunny and polite.",
        "WEATHER: Fog rolls into the Bay again. California crews give it equity and ask it to leave by noon.",
        "WEATHER: Montana reports big sky, as advertised. Surveyors measure it at \"very big.\"",
        "WEATHER: East of the Mississippi: unknown. Radios report a steady hum, possibly humid.",
        "CLASSIFIEDS: For sale, one parachute, used once, gently. Repacked by a professional. Call Tonopah.",
        "FOR SALE: Pickup truck, 300,000 miles, two tailgates, one working radio. Kearney. Serious offers and pie only.",
        "CLASSIFIEDS: Roommate wanted, Palo Alto garage. Shared desk, shared dreams, shared extension cord. Equity negotiable.",
        "FOR SALE: Large hangar near Groom Lake. Never held a Prototype. Do not ask about the Prototype.",
        "CLASSIFIEDS: Wanted: someone to tell the Boneyard's oldest bomber it's retired. It keeps trying to taxi.",
        "HELP WANTED: Radar watcher, Cheyenne Mountain. Must love blips. Snacks provided, if you hide them from Pan.",
        "HELP WANTED: Fry sauce taster, Salt Lake City. Refined palate and own napkins required. Shifts start early.",
        "HELP WANTED: Lighthouse keeper, Oregon coast. Must tolerate fog, foghorns and seagulls with opinions.",
        "LETTERS: To whoever keeps flying over my sorghum at 2 a.m.: the crop is not impressed, and neither am I. -Enid",
        "LETTERS: Must the Longhorn fly directly over the drive-in? We missed the whole movie. Twice. -Lubbock",
        "LETTERS: I would like to formally comment on the length of the public comment period. -Portland",
        "LETTERS: Thank you to the pilot who parachuted into my yard and fixed my gate before walking home. -Provo",
        "LETTERS: Mountain Time is the only real time. Everyone else is just guessing. -A Denver reader",
        "LETTERS: Who owns Lake Tahoe? California says California. Nevada says the house. The trout say leave us out of it.",
        "LOST & FOUND: Found, one very small tiara near the Last Server Farm. Owner says it fell off \"during a pivot.\"",
        "LOST: Ranger hat, wide brim, extremely damp. Last seen floating down the Columbia. Reward: a thermos of coffee.",
        "FOUND: One drone, still buzzing, stuck in a Fresno almond tree. It seems happy there. Please advise.",
        "FOUND: Small silver disk that hums, near Ely. Returned to Dreamland, who say they have never seen it before.",
        "LOST: One squeaky football, well chewed. Please return to Coach Tank. He says it's \"for practice.\"",
        "SPORTS: Abilene High wins homecoming 42-7. Coach Tank calls it \"sloppy\" and orders two-a-days through spring.",
        "SPORTS: Reno hosts its blackjack tournament. Every round won by the house. Organizers call it \"tradition.\"",
        "SPORTS: Fargo ice-fishing league resumes. Biggest catch so far: a floatplane pontoon nobody will claim.",
        "SPORTS: Seattle kayak regatta postponed due to excellent weather. Organizers \"didn't know what to do.\"",
        "SPORTS: Moab hosts its first Rock Climbing for Pilots clinic. Bring chalk. Leave the jets.",
        "SPORTS: Billings rodeo crowns a new champion. The bull has requested a rematch.",
        "RECIPE: Fry sauce. Two parts mayo, one part ketchup, one part Utah pride. Stir clockwise. Biscuit insists.",
        "RECIPE: Hotdish. Brown it, layer it, top it with tater tots, bake till the neighbors smell it. Serves twelve.",
        "RECIPE: Texas brisket. Step one: start yesterday. Step two: wait. Step three: argue with a neighbor about wood.",
        "RECIPE: Green chile stew, Gallup Truck Stop style. Ingredients: green chile. Heat level: yes.",
        "RECIPE: Colorado trail mix. Peanuts, raisins, chocolate. Remove chocolate if Pan is nearby. Pan is always nearby.",
        "RECIPE: Huckleberry pancakes. Pick huckleberries. Get rained on. Make pancakes. Eat inside. It's still raining.",
        "COMMUNITY: Gallup Truck Stop hosts Route 66 Night. Free coffee for anyone who's driven the whole road. Nobody has.",
        "COMMUNITY: Volunteers needed to rewind the World's Largest Ball of Twine after last week's scare. Bring gloves.",
        "COMMUNITY: Boise Library's potato reading club meets Tuesdays. Every book on the list is about potatoes.",
        "COMMUNITY: Old Faithful erupts on schedule again. Utah pilots have asked to study its methods.",
        "COMMUNITY: Hoover Dam tours resume Monday. Please don't touch the big switch. The Strip needs the big switch.",
        "COMMUNITY: Kingman Truck Stop pie contest this weekend. Judges: four long-haul truckers and one honest coyote.",
        "COMMUNITY: A cat in Spokane has declared independence from all seven states. She holds one windowsill so far.",
        "COMMUNITY: Mitchell's Corn Palace redecorated for the season. This year's theme: corn. Crowds are thrilled.",
        "COMMUNITY: St. George hits 112 degrees. Residents call it \"warmish\" and bring a light cardigan, just in case.",
        "REAL ESTATE: Charming Palo Alto garage. One parking spot, zero cars, three startups. Asking price: your runway.",
        "REAL ESTATE: Cozy cabin near Bend. Rain view from every window. Moss included at no extra charge.",
        "REAL ESTATE: Wyoming ranch, 40,000 acres, two cows, one neighbor. He's 90 miles away and waves anyway.",
        "REAL ESTATE: Las Vegas penthouse, neon view. Lights never go off unless someone hits the dam. Don't hit the dam.",
        "HOROSCOPE: Corgi rising. A long-awaited rain arrives, then a stranger asking about your soil. Lend a trowel.",
        "HOROSCOPE: Your lucky number is whatever Lucky says it is. Trust the house. The house trusts no one.",
        "HOROSCOPE: Retriever moon. Today is a great day to be early. You already are. Good job.",
        "ROAD REPORT: Route 66 open from Kingman to Tucumcari. Tumbleweed delays near Gallup. Truck stop pie: excellent.",
        "BUSINESS: Boneyard planes now sold by the pound. Some still run. Some just look like they'd like to.",
        "SCIENCE: White Sands Mass Driver test-fires a sack of sand. It lands at White Sands. Scientists call it a loop.",
        "RADIO: The Static hummed in a new key Tuesday. The Cheyenne ham radio club calls it \"big news, mildly spooky.\"",
        "CORRECTION: Yesterday's Sentinel said Dreamland's Prototype \"was seen.\" It was not seen. It does not exist.",
        "WEATHER: Four Corners clear and calm tonight. Chance of a giant tennis ball by morning: 100%.",
        "NOTICES: Bark Park fence inspected and rated \"extremely boingy.\" No further questions at this time.",
        "CLASSIFIEDS: FOUND: forty-one tennis balls in the Bark Park pond. Claim at the picnic table.",
        "LETTERS: \"Is it a dog park or a superweapon?\" Both, say park staff. Mostly a dog park.",
        "TOURISM: Four Corners marker adds a fifth corner. Staff say it's for the launcher.",
        "SPORTS: Big Fetch distance record stands at \"yes.\" Officials still hunting for a long enough tape.",
        "PARKS: Picnic tables are first come, first served. Utah has already reserved all of them.",
        "REAL ESTATE: Four Corners lot. Four views, one fence, zero bombs. Not for sale. Ask anyway.",
    ],
